course: dictionary
lesson: 11201
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word wizard is a good example. «The old wizard raised his staff and the stars began to spin.» The clues are staff, stars and spin, so a wizard here is a man in a story with magic powers.
explain: Now read this: «Priya is a wizard at maths, she solved the puzzle in seconds.» There are no spells here. Wizard means someone who is extremely good at something. Always check the clues around the word before you choose a meaning.
explain: Old British books sometimes used wizard as a word of praise. «Wizard!» shouted the boy, when his team won the match. The exclamation mark and the happy moment are your clues: it means excellent, and it has nothing to do with magic.
explain: Context works well, but a dictionary can settle it. «O great wizard, what is the sense of returning to me my Palace if at the same time you slay me with mirth!» Suleiman is speaking to a wizard, and mirth means laughter, so he is joking that the laughter nearly kills him.
fact: A word can have several meanings, so always check the context before you decide.
fact: «Wizard» can mean a magician in a story, someone who is extremely good at something, or a step-by-step helper in a computer program.
fact: A setup wizard on a computer guides you through the steps one at a time.
fact: In old British school stories, «Wizard!» meant excellent or great.
fact: «Mirth» means laughter, and «slay» means to kill.
exercise: «The wizard waved his wand, and the frog turned into a prince.» What is a wizard in this sentence? | A kind old teacher | A very clever maths student | A computer helper that guides you through steps | *A magician in a story with magic powers
exercise: Sam says, «I am a wizard at football!» What does wizard mean here? | A step-by-step helper | *Someone extremely good at something | A person who casts spells | Very slow at running
exercise: «The setup wizard showed me each step to install the game.» What is the wizard? | A type of board game | A wise old king | A magic man with a wand | *A computer helper that guides you step by step
test: «Wizard!» shouted Tom in the old school story, when his friend scored the winning goal. What does wizard mean here? | Tired | Dangerous | Lost | *Excellent
test: Maya is a wizard with paint, and her pictures look almost real. What does wizard mean here? | A helper inside a computer | A painter who uses magic | *Extremely good at something | Careless with colours
exam: Suleiman says, «O great wizard... you slay me with mirth!» What does mirth mean? | Sleepiness | Hunger | *Laughter | Anger
